&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9009&quot; title=&quot;Local continuous query listeners may be called on partition reassignment&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-9009&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-9009&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Don&apos;t process backup updates for local continuous queries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;hr /&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16563631" author="dmekhanikov" created="Tue, 31 Jul 2018 13:03:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Please review my patch: &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/4403&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/4403&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;TC: &lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=IgniteTests24Java8&amp;amp;branch_IgniteTests24Java8=pull%2F4403%2Fhead&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/project.html?projectId=IgniteTests24Java8&amp;amp;branch_IgniteTests24Java8=pull%2F4403%2Fhead&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16577873" author="amashenkov" created="Mon, 13 Aug 2018 06:16:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Answered on dev list &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;http://apache-ignite-developers.2346864.n4.nabble.com/Backup-queue-for-local-continuous-query-tp33391.html&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16578238" author="agoncharuk" created="Mon, 13 Aug 2018 12:51:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dmekhanikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dmekhanikov&quot;&gt;dmekhanikov&lt;/a&gt;, can you check if current implementation allows gaps in notifications? Consider the following scenario:&lt;br/&gt;
1) Register local-only continuous query&lt;br/&gt;
2) Run N updates on key K1&lt;br/&gt;
3) Block ACKs, immediately stop primary node&lt;br/&gt;
4) Check if backup receives notifications for the updated keys&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If we receive the notification on step (4), then your change is incorrect, because it will result in missing notifications for some keys during updates.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16603078" author="dmekhanikov" created="Tue, 4 Sep 2018 13:53:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt;, backups won&apos;t be notified, because they don&apos;t store the event queue. There are no ACKs sent to the backups.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think, local continuous queries should work in isolation from each other.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If processing of cache events locally on all primary nodes is required, then &lt;a href=&quot;https://ignite.apache.org/releases/latest/javadoc/org/apache/ignite/cache/query/ContinuousQuery.html#setRemoteFilter-org.apache.ignite.cache.CacheEntryEventSerializableFilter-&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;ContinuousQuery#remoteFilter&lt;/a&gt;&#160;should be used.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16603090" author="agoncharuk" created="Tue, 4 Sep 2018 14:07:12 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dmekhanikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dmekhanikov&quot;&gt;dmekhanikov&lt;/a&gt;, please update &lt;tt&gt;ContinuousQuery#setLocal&lt;/tt&gt; javadoc to state the fact that some CQ notifications may be missed during node failures when this flag is used.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16603134" author="dmekhanikov" created="Tue, 4 Sep 2018 14:49:53 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt;, done. Please take a look.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16665317" author="ignitetcbot" created="Fri, 26 Oct 2018 15:44:34 +0000"  >&lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; style=&quot;border-color: #ccc;border-style: dashed;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;panelHeader&quot; style=&quot;border-bottom-width: 1px;border-bottom-style: dashed;border-bottom-color: #ccc;background-color: #D6F7C1;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;No blockers found!&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
